<ArticleLayout title="Editorial policy" description="Our standards for independence, sourcing, authorship, updates, corrections, comparisons, and financial YMYL content.">
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>Child Savings Lab is an independent educational site. It is not part of the U.S. government, the Trump Accounts program, an investment adviser, a tax firm, or a law firm.</p>
  <h2>Evidence</h2>
  <p>Material federal-rule claims should link to primary government material. We label final guidance, form instructions, technical releases, and proposed regulations distinctly. Publication and verification dates are not interchangeable.</p>
  <h2>Authorship and review</h2>
  <p>We do not invent people, credentials, or professional review. Until a real CPA, CFP professional, attorney, or benefits specialist reviews content, we will not claim such review.</p>
  <h2>Comparisons and monetization</h2>
  <p>Purpose and user fit—not commission—determine comparison structure. If affiliate relationships are added later, they will be disclosed near relevant links and will not purchase rankings.</p>
  <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
  <p>Substantive corrections should update the underlying rule, affected tools, tests, page copy, and verification date. Readers may report issues through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
